  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nWith high pressure now off to the east, most ridge tops have \nobserved a light wind into the first part of the early morning hours,\nkeeping temperatures in the upper 40s to lower 50s. Dewpoint \ndepressions are also in the 10-20 degree range. Therefore, most frost\ndevelopment is likely limited to area valleys and portions of \ncentral Ohio, which is closer to the center of the high pressure.\n\nHigh temperatures are a few degrees warmer than yesterday, climbing\nup toward the 70 degree mark. The high pressure positioned across the\nNortheast US into the Ohio Valley shifts farther to the east, but\nanother high pressure will drop down into the Great Lakes tonight\ninto Tuesday morning. This high pressure will reinforce the dry and\nseasonal conditions through the rest of the week. \n\nThere could still be a few areas that see frost Tuesday morning, but\nin collaboration with surrounding offices, will hold off on any \nadditional headlines until later today.",
